73</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krebs</surname><given-names>HI</given-names></name><name><surname>Volpe</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Robot-aided neurorehabilitation: from evidence-based to science-based rehabilitation</article-title><source>Top Stroke Rehabil</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>54</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14523730</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fasoli</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Krebs</surname><given-names>HI</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Frontera</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of robotic therapy on motor impairment and recovery in chronic stroke</article-title><source>Archives of Phys Med Rehabil</source><year>2003</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>82</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loureiro</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Harwin</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Amirabdollahian</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Bien Z, Stefanov D</surname></name></person-group><article-title>A Gentle/s Approach to Robot Assisted Neuro-Rehabilitation</article-title><source>Advances in Rehabilitation Robotics: Human Friendly Technologies on Movement Assistance and Restoration for People with Disabilities Lecture Notes in Control and Information Sciences</source><year>2004</year><volume>306</volume><publisher-name>Germany:Springer</publisher-name><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>363</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fugl-Meyer</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaasko</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Leyman</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Steglind</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The post-stroke hemiplegic patient. 1. A method for evaluation of physical performance</article-title><source>Scand J Rehabil Med</source><year>1975</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1135616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Legg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Langhorne</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Therapy-based rehabilitation for stroke patients living at home</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2004</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1022</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14988566</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dhurjaty</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Challenges of Telerehabilitation in the Home Environment</article-title><source>Proceedings of the State of the Science Conference on Telerehabilitation</source><publisher-name>Washington DC</publisher-name><comment>12-13 October, 2001</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Winters</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>UniTherapy: A Computer-Assisted Motivating Neurorehabilitation Platform for Teleassessment and Remote Therapy</article-title><source>Proceedings of International Conference on Rehabilitation Robotics (ICORR)</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Chicago, IL</publisher-name><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>352</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Trickey</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Brauer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>TheraDrive: A New Stroke Therapy Concept for Home-based, Computer-Assisted Motivating Rehabilitation</article-title><source>Proceedings of the IEEE EMBC</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>San Francisco, USA</publisher-name><fpage>4844</fpage><lpage>47</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Winters</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of Tracking Performance Using Joystick Manipulators That Engage Different Arm Workspaces</article-title><source>Proceedings of International Conference on Rehabilitation Robotics (ICORR)</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Chicago, IL</publisher-name><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>90</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heck</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacey</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Prentza</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Peruchon</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabischong</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Katevas N</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Human-machine-interfacing for control in healthcare robots</article-title><source>Mobile Robotics in Healthcare Assistive Technology Research Series</source><year>2001</year><volume>7</volume><publisher-name>Amsterdam (Netherlands): IOS press</publisher-name><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>71</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Driessen</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Evers</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Woerden</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Manus&#x02013;a wheelchair-mounted rehabilitation robot</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Institution of Mechanical Engineers, Part H: Journal of Engineering in Medicine</source><year>2001</year><volume>215</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>90</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van der Loos</surname><given-names>HFM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Smaby</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Madrigal</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Leifer</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Khatib</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Provar assistive robot system architecture. In Robotics and Automation</article-title><source>Proceedings of IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation Detroit</source><year>1999</year><fpage>741</fpage><lpage>746</lpage><comment>2-7 May, 1999</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><